  triage:title "Hermes bridge reimplements Rust-owned validation/rendering instead of using typed AI.18 surface" ;
  triage:description "Three connected req-qa/ruthless-boundary-qa findings: ATM-QA-003 sprint doc claims bridge calls AI.18 hermes_chat_key binding (doesn't exist); RBQA-F002 re-validates segments already done via PyAgentAddress.to_typed(); RBQA-F003 manually derives agent:chat_id@team vs PyAgentAddress.__str__(). Root cause: bridge uses getattr() and local hermes_chat_key() instead of typing inputs as PyAgentAddress/PyNudge and using str(source)." ;
